# The relay is written on Windows and runs on Linux, so what is stored here has
# to be LF regardless of who commits it. That is already true, but only because
# every contributor so far has had core.autocrlf on - this makes it a property
# of the repository instead of a property of the machine.
#
# It matters beyond tidiness: a stray CR reaching the VPS is how a .env line
# stopped parsing (see tryLoadDotenv), and a CR in a config the box reads is the
# same class of problem.
* text=auto eol=lf

# binaries, which must never be touched
*.png binary
*.woff2 binary
*.exe binary
*.bz2 binary
*.onnx binary
